INT. NIGHT FERRY - CAR DECK - NIGHT

A cavernous steel hold. Dozens of parked cars bolted to the deck. The engine thrums through the floor. Chains rattle. A single bulb sways overhead.

DETECTIVE ISAAC MORROW, forties, trench coat, hand on his holster, walks slowly between the cars. At the end of the row, LIONEL FARR, thirties, in a leather jacket, leans on the bonnet of a black sedan, arms crossed. He looks at Isaac. He does not move.

ISAAC
Lionel.

LIONEL
Isaac.

ISAAC
You're a long way from home.

LIONEL
So are you.

Isaac stops ten feet away. Lionel uncrosses his arms, hands open, empty.

ISAAC
Where's the ledger?

LIONEL
Where's your warrant?

ISAAC
I don't need one on a boat.

LIONEL
You do if I'm in international waters.

ISAAC
We're nine miles out.

LIONEL
Twelve is the limit.

Isaac says nothing. The hull groans. A wave slaps the steel. The bulb swings over their faces, light, shadow, light.

LIONEL (CONT'D)
You came alone.

ISAAC
So did you.

LIONEL
Not exactly.

Behind Isaac, a car door clunks. He spins, gun half drawn. Nobody. Lionel laughs.

LIONEL (CONT'D)
Relax. It's the sea.

Isaac turns back. His hand shakes slightly. He steadies it.

ISAAC
Hand over the ledger and I let you walk off in Calais.

LIONEL
And if I don't?

ISAAC
Then I walk off. And you don't.

Lionel studies him. A long moment. He reaches slowly into his jacket. Isaac draws. Lionel freezes, hand inside his coat.

ISAAC (CONT'D)
Slow.

LIONEL
I'm slow.

He draws out a small black book. Holds it up between two fingers.

LIONEL (CONT'D)
Here.

ISAAC
Toss it.

Lionel tosses it. It lands at Isaac's feet. Isaac kneels, picks it up, flips through. His shoulders drop an inch.

ISAAC (CONT'D)
It's blank.

LIONEL
Of course it's blank.

Isaac looks up, furious. Lionel is already laughing, the sound ricocheting off the steel. Isaac lowers the gun, then, slowly, he begins to laugh too. Two men in a steel hold, laughing at a blank book.

ISAAC
You're a bastard, Lionel.

LIONEL
And you're still a detective.

He pushes off the sedan and walks past Isaac toward the stairs. Isaac lets him go.
